From: Timofey Maykov <itnitro@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: pcs: qcom-ipq9574: optional early 10G-QXGMII bring-up before the PHY package

The vendor SSDK brings the SoC UNIPHY up first and configures the QCA8084
package afterwards, when the SoC side already transmits. Two of its own
commits (3c58ee12 "initialize manhattan after enabling miami uniphy",
b729483c "configure mht uqxgmii when exit erp") describe the opposite
order as "mht serdes 10g link up and xpcs uniphy autoneg timeout", which
is what the failing BE7000 boards log: the QCA8084 locks, the SoC never
does and its in-band AN times out. In this tree the PHY package is
configured at PHY attach (about 12 s), the PCS only when phylink starts
the port (about 23 s). A board that works had the UNIPHY still running
from the previous boot at attach time.

When the DT node carries qcom,early-10g-qxgmii, configure UNIPHY0 for
10G-QXGMII at probe, so it transmits before the package is set up. The
later phylink config sees the interface already set and only does the
per-channel part.

diff --git a/drivers/net/pcs/pcs-qcom-ipq9574.c b/drivers/net/pcs/pcs-qcom-ipq9574.c
index f500c9a..54cfdfe 100644
--- a/drivers/net/pcs/pcs-qcom-ipq9574.c
+++ b/drivers/net/pcs/pcs-qcom-ipq9574.c
@@ -1642,6 +1642,20 @@ static int ipq9574_pcs_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 				    &ipq_pcs_regs_fops);
 	}
 
+	/* Vendor order. The SSDK brings the SoC UNIPHY up first and configures
+	 * the QCA8084 package only when the SoC side already transmits; its
+	 * own commits say the other way round "will see mht serdes 10g link up
+	 * and xpcs uniphy autoneg timeout", which is exactly what the failing
+	 * BE7000 boards log. Here the PHY package is configured at PHY attach,
+	 * long before phylink configures this PCS, so when the DT asks for it
+	 * bring UNIPHY0 up for 10G-QXGMII right away. phylink's later config
+	 * finds the interface already set and only does the per-channel part.
+	 */
+	if (of_property_read_bool(dev->of_node, "qcom,early-10g-qxgmii")) {
+		ret = ipq_pcs_config_usxgmii(qpcs, 0, PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_10G_QXGMII);
+		dev_info(dev, "early 10G-QXGMII bring-up before the PHY package: %d\n", ret);
+	}
+
 	platform_set_drvdata(pdev, qpcs);
 
 	return 0;
